1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,997
During severe weather, travelers may not know which
warning to trust, or where to find reliable help.

2
00:00:08,997 --> 00:00:15,347
StormSignal brings official warnings and local
guidance together in one simple view.

3
00:00:16,347 --> 00:00:30,190
Chennai is our demo district. Switch between English,
Tamil, and Hindi for familiar safety information.

4
00:00:31,190 --> 00:00:51,986
The IMD wording reads: Thunderstorm and lightning,
squall, et cetera. Check the source date and link.

5
00:00:52,986 --> 00:01:04,744
A scheduled refresh checks the public IMD Chennai
page every 30 minutes and publishes its latest snapshot.

6
00:01:05,744 --> 00:01:15,625
This is district-level forecast information, not
street-by-street conditions. No verified shelters

7
00:01:15,625 --> 00:01:20,116
or safe routes are shown.

8
00:01:21,116 --> 00:01:36,532
For thunder, move indoors, stay away from windows
and plumbing, and shelter for 30 minutes after

9
00:01:36,532 --> 00:01:39,423
the last thunder.

10
00:01:40,423 --> 00:01:49,268
If the source is old or unavailable, the app says
it cannot verify the current warning. No warning

11
00:01:49,268 --> 00:01:51,726
listed is not an all-clear.

12
00:01:52,726 --> 00:02:09,712
Chennai help: Disaster Helpline 1077 and Corporation
1913. Verify the numbers with District Administration.

13
00:02:10,712 --> 00:02:23,215
StormSignal makes official warnings easier to
understand. In an emergency, follow local authorities.

